On Express 4, a handler that throws never sends a response, so `'finish'` never fires and the failed request leaves no log line. That is the case you'd most want to see.

What matters most is where the logs go. If you already run a log pipeline, use its Express integration (for example `pino-http`) in place of `console.log`. Which stack do you use?

